RULES:
At the first of two decisions, only player 1 reads public_label, both players read private_banner and counter, and only player 0 reads token. The names public_label and private_banner do not grant or restrict access. Between decisions, player 1 puts the SAME public_label value on an open tray where BOTH can read it at decision two. Other permissions do not change. One model must cover both decisions with these exact four field names. Other fields do not encode any private value; without the explicitly stated display a player cannot infer a field assigned only to the other player.
FIELDS: {"counter": "common counter", "private_banner": "banner on the common wall", "public_label": "label printed inside a sealed pocket", "token": "personal token"}
